---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<Page title="How We Research" description="How we write, source, and update our pet guides and product recommendations.">
  <h2>Health and safety guides</h2>
  <p>
    Anything about food safety or pet health is based on published veterinary sources, such as the ASPCA Animal Poison
    Control Center, the Merck Veterinary Manual, the U.S. FDA Center for Veterinary Medicine, and International Cat
    Care. Each article lists its sources at the bottom so you can read them yourself.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our guides are general information, not a diagnosis. When the right answer is "call your vet," we say so plainly.
  </p>

  <h2>Product recommendations</h2>
  <p>
    Our product picks are researched, not lab-tested. We compare manufacturer specifications, sizing and materials,
    recall history, return policies, and patterns across large numbers of owner reviews, then explain who each product
    is (and isn't) a good fit for. When we have personally used a product, we say so in the article. If we haven't,
    we don't pretend otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>How our articles are written</h2>
  <p>
    Our articles are researched and drafted with AI tools, following strict sourcing rules: every health claim must
    come from a veterinary or other reputable source that we cite, and each article is checked against those sources
    before it's published. If you spot a mistake, tell us and we'll fix it.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Each article shows when it was last updated. We review popular articles regularly and fix errors as soon as we
    find them. Spot something wrong? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    Some links earn us a commission. That never decides what we recommend. See our
    <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
